{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121814","id":4139204257,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc72tz6h","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121814","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121814.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121814.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121814","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121814/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121814/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121814/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/cb88c8e5021ba7a704cffade2cf9f28d1f3db777","number":121814,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix exponential ratio of `Range` when `min_value` is zero","user":{"login":"Kyzzsa","id":53786793,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNzg2Nzkz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53786793?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa","html_url":"https://github.com/Kyzzsa","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nWhen `exp_edit` is enabled on a `Range` node and `min_value` is set to `0`, setting `ratio` to `0` currently yields a `value` of `1`. Moreover, if `min_value` is `0` and `max_value` is less than `1`, the slider becomes completely unusable.\r\n\r\nThis happens because the internal mapping treats `0` as `1` to avoid undefined behaviour of `log(0)`, which brings the inconsistency. The solution is to shift the range with a small positive epsilon before taking the logarithm when `min_value` is zero, and then shift the value back. The chosen epsilon (`1e-3`) is the same as the default step of `EditorSpinSlider`, which avoids a steep curve and unintended non‑zero values displayed as zero.\r\n\r\n- Closes #121804\r\n- Closes #109248\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThis PR also removes a redundant calculation in `ProgressBar`, and the fix only affects `Range` and its child classes, specifically when `min_value` is exactly `0`.\r\n\r\nThis PR implements one of the approaches discussed in #121804.\r\n\r\nTests were done on MRPs from #121804 and #109248, and worked as expected.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1732720779,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzMyNzIwNzc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gui","name":"topic:gui","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","number":25,"state":"open","title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url